{
  "id": "claude-managed",
  "label": "Claude Code: managed settings (administrator enforcement)",
  "tool": "claude-code",
  "scope": "machine",
  "requires_admin": true,
  "selectors": [
    "claude",
    "claude-managed",
    "managed"
  ],
  "enforcement": {
    "windows": "hard",
    "linux": "advisory",
    "darwin": "advisory"
  },
  "$comment": [
    "Settings precedence, from highest to lowest:",
    "  managed -> command line -> .claude/settings.local.json",
    "  -> .claude/settings.json -> ~/.claude/settings.json",
    "",
    "'hard' on Windows because the developer is not a local admin there. On Ubuntu/macOS the developer",
    "has root access and can edit /etc, so there it provides friction + auditability, not",
    "containment: the installer summary prints this difference.",
    "",
    "Overwrite strategy: these files are ours, there is no developer customization",
    "to preserve. If someone edited them, that is precisely what we want to",
    "overwrite during scheduled reapplies."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "DIRECT CONSEQUENCE of allowManagedPermissionRulesOnly=true: permission rules in ~/.claude/settings.json of ALL users are IGNORED by the CLI: including those written by this package in the user layer. Only this managed source applies. CLAUDE.md continues to function normally.",
    "allowManagedHooksOnly=true disables any hook declared in user settings. If any team depends on custom hooks, they must be included here.",
    "allowManagedHooksOnly=true also disables statusLine declared in user settings without warning. Therefore, the package statusLine comes from here: it is the only source the CLI accepts under this flag. Developers who had custom statuslines lose them: if any team depends on one, it must be added here.",
    "Managed CLAUDE.md and ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md are CONCATENATED by the CLI, not overwritten. Therefore, the user target declares superseded_by pointing here: with this file present, the user block is removed, paying the core cost once per prompt.",
    "This file is being REMOVED, not written. While present, Claude Code takes exclusive MCP control: it loads only what is here and rejects 'claude mcp add' with 'enterprise MCP configuration is active and has exclusive control over MCP servers'. With no published AI policy, locking the developer is friction without mandate. Semgrep arrives via ~/.claude.json; Trivy remains a CLI because its MCP depends on an unpinned, unverified plugin. Developers add the rest with 'claude mcp add'. To block a specific server without closing the entire surface, use deniedMcpServers in managed-settings.json."
  ],
  "files": [
    {
      "dest": {
        "windows": "${PROGRAMFILES}/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.json",
        "linux": "/etc/claude-code/managed-settings.json",
        "darwin": "/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-settings.json"
      },
      "format": "json",
      "strategy": "overwrite",
      "backup": true,
      "payload": {
        "permissions": {
          "disableBypassPermissionsMode": "disable",
          "allowManagedPermissionRulesOnly": true,
          "deny": [
            "Read(**/.env)",
            "Edit(**/.env)",
            "Read(**/.env.*)",
            "Edit(**/.env.*)",
            "Read(**/secrets/**)",
            "Edit(**/secrets/**)",
            "Read(**/credentials/**)",
            "Edit(**/credentials/**)",
            "Read(**/id_rsa)",
            "Edit(**/id_rsa)",
            "Read(**/id_ed25519)",
            "Edit(**/id_ed25519)",
            "Read(**/*.key)",
            "Edit(**/*.key)",
            "Read(**/*.pem)",
            "Edit(**/*.pem)",
            "Read(**/*.p12)",
            "Edit(**/*.p12)",
            "Read(**/*.pfx)",
            "Edit(**/*.pfx)",
            "Read(**/*.jks)",
            "Edit(**/*.jks)",
            "Read(**/*.kdbx)",
            "Edit(**/*.kdbx)",
            "Read(~/.ssh/**)",
            "Edit(~/.ssh/**)",
            "Read(//c/Users/**/.ssh/**)",
            "Edit(//c/Users/**/.ssh/**)",
            "Read(//home/**/.ssh/**)",
            "Edit(//home/**/.ssh/**)",
            "Read(//Users/**/.ssh/**)",
            "Edit(//Users/**/.ssh/**)",
            "Read(~/.aws/**)",
            "Edit(~/.aws/**)",
            "Read(//c/Users/**/.aws/**)",
            "Edit(//c/Users/**/.aws/**)",
            "Read(//home/**/.aws/**)",
            "Edit(//home/**/.aws/**)",
            "Read(//Users/**/.aws/**)",
            "Edit(//Users/**/.aws/**)",
            "Read(~/.azure/**)",
            "Edit(~/.azure/**)",
            "Read(~/.config/gcloud/**)",
            "Edit(~/.config/gcloud/**)",
            "Read(~/.gnupg/**)",
            "Edit(~/.gnupg/**)",
            "Read(//c/Users/**/.gnupg/**)",
            "Edit(//c/Users/**/.gnupg/**)",
            "Read(//home/**/.gnupg/**)",
            "Edit(//home/**/.gnupg/**)",
            "Read(//Users/**/.gnupg/**)",
            "Edit(//Users/**/.gnupg/**)",
            "Read(~/.kube/**)",
            "Edit(~/.kube/**)",
            "Read(//c/Users/**/.kube/**)",
            "Edit(//c/Users/**/.kube/**)",
            "Read(//home/**/.kube/**)",
            "Edit(//home/**/.kube/**)",
            "Read(//Users/**/.kube/**)",
            "Edit(//Users/**/.kube/**)",
            "Read(~/.docker/config.json)",
            "Edit(~/.docker/config.json)",
            "Read(~/.git-credentials)",
            "Edit(~/.git-credentials)",
            "Read(~/.netrc)",
            "Edit(~/.netrc)",
            "Read(~/.npmrc)",
            "Edit(~/.npmrc)",
            "Read(~/.pypirc)",
            "Edit(~/.pypirc)",
            "Read(~/.terraform.d/credentials.tfrc.json)",
            "Edit(~/.terraform.d/credentials.tfrc.json)",
            "Bash(chmod 777:*)",
            "Bash(git push --force:*)",
            "Bash(git config --global core.hooksPath:*)",
            "Bash(git commit --no-verify:*)",
            "Bash(git push -f:*)",
            "Bash(git filter-branch:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl get secret:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl get secrets:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl describe secret:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl describe secrets:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl create token:*)"
          ],
          "ask": [
            "Bash(python:*)",
            "Bash(python3:*)",
            "Bash(node:*)",
            "Bash(npx:*)",
            "Bash(terraform apply:*)",
            "Bash(sudo:*)",
            "Bash(curl:*)",
            "Bash(wget:*)",
            "Bash(npm audit fix:*)",
            "Bash(npm install:*)",
            "Bash(npm update:*)",
            "Bash(pnpm:*)",
            "Bash(yarn:*)",
            "Bash(bun:*)",
            "Bash(pipx:*)",
            "Bash(poetry:*)",
            "Bash(uv:*)",
            "Bash(npm install -g:*)",
            "Bash(pip install:*)",
            "Bash(docker run:*)",
            "Bash(docker build:*)",
            "Bash(docker push:*)",
            "Bash(docker rm:*)",
            "Bash(docker rmi:*)",
            "Bash(docker exec:*)",
            "Bash(docker logs:*)",
            "Bash(docker inspect:*)",
            "Bash(docker compose logs:*)",
            "Bash(docker compose up:*)",
            "Bash(docker compose down:*)",
            "Bash(docker system prune:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl apply:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl delete:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl exec:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl scale:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl rollout:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl port-forward:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl get:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl describe:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl logs:*)",
            "Bash(terraform destroy:*)",
            "Bash(terraform import:*)",
            "Bash(terraform state rm:*)",
            "Bash(terraform plan:*)",
            "Bash(terraform show:*)",
            "Bash(terraform output:*)",
            "Bash(aws iam:*)",
            "Bash(aws s3 rm:*)",
            "Bash(aws s3 sync:*)",
            "Bash(aws ec2 terminate-instances:*)",
            "Bash(aws cloudformation delete-stack:*)",
            "Bash(git push:*)",
            "Bash(git commit:*)",
            "Bash(git clone:*)",
            "Bash(git config --global:*)",
            "Bash(git submodule update:*)",
            "Bash(git reset --hard:*)",
            "Bash(git clean:*)",
            "Bash(git rebase:*)",
            "Bash(git restore:*)",
            "Bash(git branch -D:*)",
            "Bash(git branch -d:*)",
            "Bash(git tag -d:*)",
            "Bash(git remote add:*)",
            "Bash(git remote set-url:*)",
            "Bash(git remote remove:*)",
            "Bash(git stash drop:*)",
            "Bash(git stash clear:*)"
          ],
          "allow": [
            "Bash(git status:*)",
            "Bash(git diff:*)",
            "Bash(git log:*)",
            "Bash(git add:*)",
            "Bash(git branch:*)",
            "Bash(npm run:*)",
            "Bash(npm test:*)",
            "Bash(docker ps:*)",
            "Bash(docker images:*)",
            "Bash(semgrep:*)",
            "Bash(trivy:*)",
            "Bash(gitleaks:*)",
            "Bash(npm audit:*)",
            "Bash(docker version:*)",
            "Bash(docker compose ps:*)",
            "Bash(kubectl config current-context:*)",
            "Bash(terraform validate:*)",
            "Bash(terraform fmt:*)",
            "Bash(aws sts get-caller-identity:*)",
            "Bash(aws s3 ls:*)",
            "Bash(aws ec2 describe-:*)",
            "Bash(aws logs describe-:*)",
            "Bash(git show:*)",
            "Bash(git fetch:*)",
            "Bash(git remote -v:*)",
            "Bash(git stash list:*)",
            "Bash(git blame:*)",
            "Bash(git rev-parse:*)",
            "Bash(git ls-files:*)"
          ]
        },
        "allowManagedHooksOnly": true,
        "statusLine": {
          "type": "command",
          "command": "PLACEHOLDER"
        }
      },
      "payload_by_os": {
        "statusLine.command": {
          "windows": "python \"${PROGRAMFILES}/ClaudeCode/statusline-security.py\"",
          "linux": "python3 \"/etc/claude-code/statusline-security.py\"",
          "darwin": "python3 \"/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/statusline-security.py\""
        }
      },
      "$notes": []
    },
    {
      "dest": {
        "windows": "${PROGRAMFILES}/ClaudeCode/managed-mcp.json",
        "linux": "/etc/claude-code/managed-mcp.json",
        "darwin": "/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/managed-mcp.json"
      },
      "strategy": "remove",
      "$comment": "INTENTIONALLY REMOVED, and removed from disk for anyone who previously had it. managed-mcp.json is not a server list: the presence of the file gives EXCLUSIVE control to the admin, and the CLI rejects 'claude mcp add' with 'enterprise MCP configuration is active and has exclusive control over MCP servers'. allowManagedMcpServersOnly does not control this -- it only determines whether the user allowlist is ignored. Without a published AI policy, locking down the developer is friction without mandate. The Semgrep baseline continues to arrive via ~/.claude.json (targets/claude-code.json, merge-mcp). Trivy remains a CLI until the MCP plugin has verified version and provenance. deniedMcpServers remains available to block a specific server. managedMcpServers cannot serve as a replacement: it only accepts http/sse, while our baseline is stdio (command/args/env). Revisit when an AI policy is published."
    },
    {
      "dest": {
        "windows": "${PROGRAMFILES}/ClaudeCode/statusline-security.py",
        "linux": "/etc/claude-code/statusline-security.py",
        "darwin": "/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/statusline-security.py"
      },
      "format": "text",
      "strategy": "overwrite",
      "$comment": "Statusline script. Placed in MACHINE scope because the managed-settings.json referencing it is shared across all users: an embedded user profile path would point to the home directory of whoever ran the installer.",
      "payload_file": "statusline/security-status.py"
    },
    {
      "dest": {
        "windows": "${PROGRAMFILES}/ClaudeCode/CLAUDE.md",
        "linux": "/etc/claude-code/CLAUDE.md",
        "darwin": "/Library/Application Support/ClaudeCode/CLAUDE.md"
      },
      "format": "markdown",
      "strategy": "md-block",
      "marker": "<!-- security-team-block -->",
      "$comment": "Managed policy CLAUDE.md. Unlike ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md, developers cannot delete this (requires admin) and cannot exclude it via claudeMdExcludes: official documentation states: 'Managed policy CLAUDE.md files cannot be excluded'. This is NOT hard technical enforcement: documentation notes that CLAUDE.md shapes behavior rather than acting as an enforcement layer. The adjacent managed-settings.json enforces policy.",
      "compose": [
        "policy/core-runtime.md",
        "policy/vendor-claude-code.md"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
